        "name": "pipeline_error_handler",
        "description": "Task 041 / DEC-004 Option A (amended 2026-07-27): runs on EVERY outcome of data_quality_checks - Succeeded, Failed and Skipped. Because the pipeline is a single convergent DAG and Skipped propagates transitively, this one handler covers all upstream activities. Reads per-activity outcomes via POST queryactivityruns (not @activity('X').Error, which is empty for skipped activities) and writes one gold_pipeline_execution_log row per terminal activity, successes included, so a clean run populates the log too (criterion 3). The notebook then RE-RAISES if any activity failed, which is what keeps a failing run red - without it the Try-Catch shape would report the whole run as Succeeded and silently undo task-026's DQ gate. That raise replaces the trailing Fail activity the original DEC-004 shape used.",
        "dependsOn": [
          {
            "activity": "data_quality_checks",
            "dependencyConditions": [
              "Succeeded",
              "Failed",
              "Skipped"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
